# List Loading Skeletons

Show skeletons only on **initial load** when there is no data yet:

```tsx
const showSkeleton = loading && displayedItems.length === 0;
```

Do not replace visible rows with skeletons during pagination or refresh when items already display.

## Extract a component

Prefer `<Domain>LoadingSkeleton viewMode={viewMode} />` over large inline blocks in the page file (see Users, Services).

## List view skeleton

- Container: `space-y-4`
- Each row: `Card` with flex layout matching real list cards
- Media pulse: use `LIST_CARD_LIST_MEDIA_WIDTH_CLASS` from `CardKebabTrigger`
- Placeholder blocks for title, status badge, kebab (`h-8 w-8`), detail grid, footer

## Grid view skeleton

Use the **same breakpoints** as [list-pages-card-view.mdc](mdc:.cursor/rules/list-pages-card-view.mdc):

```
grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4
```

(or `gap-6` if the live page uses `gap-6` — match the page, not a different breakpoint set)

Each card: hero/media pulse + 2–3 text line pulses.

## Styling

- Pulse blocks: `bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700 animate-pulse rounded`
- Card shell: match live cards (`p-6`, glass/border tokens when used on the real card)

## Do not

- Use `xl:grid-cols-4` when the live grid stops at `lg:grid-cols-4`
- Show skeleton and `EmptyState` simultaneously
- Fetch-specific skeleton counts are fine (6 list rows, 8 grid cards) — keep consistent within a page

## Reference implementations

- `front-end/src/features/users/pages/UsersPage/components/LoadingSkeleton.tsx` (preferred extracted pattern)
- `front-end/src/features/services/pages/ServicesPage/components/ServicesPageLoadingSkeleton.tsx`

## Verification

```bash
cd front-end
npm run type-check
npm run lint
```

When refactoring a page, update **both** runtime grid and skeleton grid together.
